From 14fe9a5161caffafd109b85a0757e8367d302aa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:50:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Slip verification: submit-then-poll, stage timing logs,
 document fallback

Backend: slip purchases accept ?async=1 - the wallet is debited and the
reference returned immediately while the provider call settles in the
background; GET /verification/slip/:reference reports processing / success /
failed (with the provider's reason) / review. Unexpected background errors are
parked for reconciliation (or refunded when the request never left). Every
request logs a [slip-timing] line (debit vs provider vs total) so slow stages
can be identified; Techhub gets a 60s timeout that keeps the outcome unknown
instead of refunding. Responses now carry a document_url for providers that
confirm with a download link instead of an inline PDF.

Web: all slip pages share runSlipFlow - submit, poll every 1.5s with a live
'verifying' message, show the result as soon as it is ready, never an open
request a browser/proxy can cut. The PDF button falls back to the owner's
document endpoint when no inline PDF came back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015YoLAo63RFk6PcWruuMD9h
